0,Ohlone - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ohlone,"The Muwekma Ohlone Tribe is composed of documented descendants of the historic Verona Band of Alameda County, an intertribal Ohlone-Miwok-Yokuts community. The Ohlone/Costanoan Esselen Nation, consisting of descendants of intermarried Rumsen Costanoan and Esselen speakers of Mission San Carlos Borromeo, are centered at Monterey.",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
1,Karkin people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karkin_people,"The Karkin people have historically lived in the Carquinez Strait region in the northeast portion of the San Francisco Bay estuary. [1] They spoke the Karkin language, the only documentation of which is a single vocabulary obtained by linguist-missionary Felipe Arroyo de la Cuesta at Mission Dolores in 1821 [2] from Karkin speaker Mariano Antonio Sagnegse. [3] According to de la Cuesta, karkin ...",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
2,Miwok Music Project - Sound Orchard,https://www.soundorchard.org/miwok-music-project.html,"The Miwok Music Project explores the influence of music created by the indigenous people of Northern California through community singing, language instruction, song recording and documentation, and the creation of new music rooted in Miwok culture. ""It's very very powerful to hear the Miwok language being sung out loud by so many voices through this project; bringing to life the spirit of the ...",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
3,Karkin - California Language Archive,https://cla.berkeley.edu/languages/karkin.html,"Karkin (also spelled ""Carquin"") is an Ohlone (or ""Costanoan"") language, along with Awaswas, Chalon, Chochenyo, Mutsun, Ramaytush, Rumsen, and Tamyen. The Ohlone languages comprise one branch of the hypothesized Penutian language family, within which they form a subgroup with the Miwokan languages (Central Sierra Miwok, Coast Miwok, Lake Miwok, Northern Sierra Miwok, Plains Miwok ...",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
4,Karkin Revisited - JSTOR,https://www.jstor.org/stable/1265103,"The principal sound correspondences linking Northern Costanoan to Southern Costanoan, and linking the Miwok family to the Costanoan family are presented at the end of table 1.",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
5,Miwok: Music — San Geronimo Valley Historical Society,https://www.sgvhistoricalsociety.org/miwok-music,"Music The Catherine A. Callaghan collection of Bodega Miwok sound recordings Linguistic field recordings: linguistic data; stories; ethnographic data; songs. "" Two Bodega Love Songs "" "" Feast song (Spiritual song) "" "" Two Big Head Dance songs "" Citation: Sarah Ballard and Catherine A. Callaghan.",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
6,PDF Ohlone/Costanoan Indians,https://www.npshistory.com/publications/goga/ohlone-indians.pdf,"Karkin Costanoan languages, as well as a few who spoke the same San Francisco Bay Costanoan language as the San Francisco Peninsula people (Figure 2 and Figure 3).",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
7,Miwok Sound Recording - Smithsonian Institution,https://www.si.edu/object/archives/components/sova-naa-1976-95-ref16728,"The preferred citation for the Harrington Papers will reference the actual location within the collection, i.e. Box 172, Alaska/Northwest Coast, Papers of John Peabody Harrington, National Anthropological Archives, Smithsonian Institution. However, as the NAA understands the need to cite phrases or vocabulary on specific pages, a citation referencing the microfilmed papers is acceptable ...",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
8,Lisjan (Ohlone) History & Territory - The Sogorea Te Land Trust,https://sogoreate-landtrust.org/lisjan-history-and-territory/,"The Lisjan are made up of the seven nations that were directly enslaved at Mission San Jose in Fremont, CA and Mission Dolores in San Francisco, CA: Chochenyo (Ohlone), Karkin (Ohlone), Bay Miwok, Plains Miwok, Delta Yokut and Patwin.",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
9,Tribal Territory - Association of Ramaytush Ohlone,https://www.ramaytush.org/tribal-territory.html,"Native peoples in California tend to differentiate themselves one from another by their political (""nationality,"" so to speak), ethnic (or cultural), and linguistic differences. In the San...",Karkin,Miwok-Costanoan
